cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this repository, please cite it as below. To cite the practice-based evaluation report alone, use the preferred-citation entry. NOTE: licensing is split, so no single license identifier applies to the repository as a whole. The report, survey instrument, analysis and images are CC-BY-4.0 (declared on the preferred-citation entry); the participant response data (CSV/XLSX, individual respondent PDFs, ID mapping) is released under a more restrictive research-use licence. LICENSE carries the scope note and docs/DATA_LICENSE.md the data terms."
title: "Hi-AUDiO: Practice-Based Evaluation — Report, Participant Survey, and Response Analysis"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Brown
    given-names: Nela
    affiliation: "FLO Lab, Female Laptop Orchestra"
  - name: "Hi-AUDiO"
date-released: 2026-08-21
license-url: "https://github.com/idsinge/hiaudio_FLO_practice-based_evaluation/blob/main/LICENSE"
repository-code: "https://github.com/idsinge/hiaudio_FLO_practice-based_evaluation"
url: "https://idsinge.github.io/hiaudio_FLO_practice-based_evaluation/"
abstract: >
  The published documentation of a practice-based evaluation of the Hi-Audio
  platform conducted by nine performers from the Female Laptop Orchestra (FLO): the
  evaluation report, the participant questionnaire as administered, the
  pseudonymised response data from all nine respondents (one of whom co-designed
  the questionnaire and authored the report — see its positionality note), and
  the analysis of those responses, including descriptive results, thematic
  coding of open questions, and triangulation against the report.
keywords:
  - audio
  - web audio
  - networked music performance
  - collaborative recording
  - practice-based research
  - usability evaluation
  - digital audio workstation
  - survey data
preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: "Hi-AUDiO: Practice-Based Evaluation Report"
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  authors:
    - family-names: Brown
      given-names: Nela
      affiliation: "FLO Lab, Female Laptop Orchestra"
  date-released: 2026-03-22
  abstract: >
    A practice-based evaluation of the Hi-Audio platform conducted by nine
    performers from the Female Laptop Orchestra (FLO) between February and
    March 2026, during the production of a collaborative composition for the
    Radiophrenia 2026 festival. The report assesses the platform's suitability
    for professional creative workflows and identifies design considerations
    for future development.
  notes: >
    Relates to the project Hybrid and Interpretable Deep Neural Audio Machines,
    funded by the European Research Council (ERC) under the European Union's
    Horizon Europe research and innovation programme (grant agreement No. 101052978).
